{
  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat → acc 0.507, F1 0.455, 3.95 GPU-hrs), the primary uncertainty is whether the transformer aggregation layer—the most computationally expensive component—is actually contributing to performance or simply adding overfitting risk and cost. Config_009 is a clean single-variable ablation of config_001 (transformer → avgpool, everything else identical), so any accuracy difference can be attributed to the aggregation strategy. If avgpool matches or exceeds 0.507, we can confidently drop transformer-based configs from the remaining 8 experiments, saving ~1–1.5 GPU-hrs each. If it is clearly worse, we confirm the transformer is necessary and can focus subsequent experiments on tuning around it. This is the highest-information-per-GPU-hour next step: it reduces uncertainty about the single most costly architectural choice while staying within the same multimodal + multiprofile direction. Expected relative cost: moderate (~2.5–3.0 GPU-hrs), roughly 20–30% cheaper than config_001 since avgpool is far lighter than a transformer while still processing the same heavy scgpt and ViT-L encoders."
}

